Two changes for Dukovo's sshd(8) (ADR 0347).

russh hands a server's handler what a client signed to sign in with a
public key (RFC 4252 section 7), and the signature, beside the key it
verified: sshd passes both to authd(8), which checks the signature
again itself before it starts a session as the person, so that sshd's
word alone never makes anyone a person. The fields are new, and
VerifiedPublicKey is non-exhaustive.

A handler may also give a client room to send on a channel itself, as
it consumes what came (RFC 4254 section 5.2), as OpenSSH's sshd does,
rather than russh as the data comes: otherwise a client can send
faster than a session reads, and the connection must hold all of it or
stop, and stopping holds up the session's output too. Handlers that do
not ask for it (adjusts_window) see no change.

